 ### SpatialHash3D
-The underlying spatial index structure. Reprojected indices rely on the O(1) lookup provided by SpatialHash3D for fallback computations [Parent].
+A spatial index structure using a uniform 3D hash grid to enable efficient nearest-neighbor and radius-based queries for static datasets [Parent]. It provides O(1) cell lookup and serves as the fallback mechanism when reprojection fails [Parent]. Choose it when static spatial queries are required without temporal dependencies [Parent]. [SpatialHash3D](5113-spatialhash3d.md)
 
 ### RTAO
-The shading pass that consumes the reprojected indices. The decoupling allows for optimized shading without index lookup overhead [S1, unofficial].
+A fullscreen shading pass that consumes the reprojected hash index texture to compute ambient occlusion. It is decoupled from the index computation to improve shader occupancy and reduce atomic contention. Choose it when decoupling shading from index generation improves performance. [RTAO](5114-rtao.md)
 
 ## Operating characteristics
-*   **Time Complexity**: The reprojection step is O(1) per pixel for valid history, avoiding the hash computation and atomic writes. Fallback cases remain O(1) but with higher constant factors due to atomic operations [S1, unofficial].
-*   **Memory Complexity**: The method requires storing the previous frame’s index texture, adding memory overhead proportional to the screen resolution [S1, unofficial].
